# The hxcpp arm of the Fast-parse / writer benchmark harness — the native twin of
# `tools/parse-prof.hxml`, same `tools/ParseProf.hx` source, same `src/`, same
# `-D analyzer-optimize`, so the two arms differ only in the backend.
#
# Build from the repo root; the artifact tree is gitignored. Point
# HXCPP_COMPILE_CACHE at a persistent directory or every build is a cold ~40 s:
#
#   HXCPP_COMPILE_CACHE=~/.hxcpp_cache haxe tools/bench-hxcpp.hxml
#   TM_SRC=... bin/parse-prof-cpp/ParseProf tparse tools/bench-corpus.txt 6 hxformat.json
#
# No `-lib hxnodejs`: `Sys` / `sys.io.File` are stdlib on a sys target, and the
# one js-only clock in ParseProf (`performance.now()`) is already behind `#if js`
# with a `haxe.Timer.stamp()` fallback.
-cp src
-cp tools
-main ParseProf
-D analyzer-optimize
-cpp bin/parse-prof-cpp
